Package: susine
Title: Sum of Single, Non-Central Effects (SuSiNE)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Michael G.", "Callahan", , "mgc5166@psu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-6532-0995"))
Description: Implements the Sum of Single Non-central Effects (SuSiNE) model, a
    Bayesian variable-selection and fine-mapping method that extends SuSiE by
    allowing nonzero, signed prior means on effect sizes (mu_0 = c * a, where
    'a' is an annotation-derived signed vector and 'c' a global scale). Provides
    model fitting from individual-level data ('susine()'), sufficient statistics
    ('susine_ss()'), and summary statistics / RSS ('susine_rss()'), together with
    the single-effect regression building blocks, empirical-Bayes prior-update
    methods, and multi-start fit aggregation. Returns posterior inclusion
    probabilities, credible sets, and the evidence lower bound (ELBO).
